snowplow_agent_analytics 0.2.0 (2026-11-03)
----------------------------------------
## Summary
Add BigQuery and Databricks support alongside Snowflake. This is the first tagged
release; existing installations of the untagged 0.1.0 package require a base-table
migration before upgrading.

## Features
- Read native Snowplow entity records on BigQuery and typed arrays of structs on
  Databricks, with safe handling of null and empty entity arrays.
- Use warehouse-specific incremental updates and date partitioning while retaining
  the existing attribution rules and expected Snowflake outputs.
- Keep conformed dimensions and the optional semantic view available on Snowflake
  only.

## Fixes
- Persist 19 scalar columns in `base_events` so changes to nested event entities do
  not change the stored base schema.
- Accept numeric window settings supplied as strings and preserve Monday-based
  weekly snapshots across the supported warehouses.

## Requirements
- dbt Core >=1.10.6 and <2.0.0; snowplow-utils >=1.0.1 and <2.0.0.
- Databricks requires dbt-databricks >=1.11 and a SQL warehouse or Runtime 12.2 LTS
  or later. Incremental tables use Delta.
- Set `snowplow__license_accepted: true` after accepting the Snowplow Personal and
  Academic License or confirming your commercial agreement with Snowplow.
- Redshift and standalone Spark are not supported in this release.

## Upgrading
Existing Snowflake installations with raw entity columns in `base_events` must
migrate that table before running the new version. The schema guard rejects an
unmigrated table.

Follow the [Agent Analytics migration guide](https://docs.snowplow.io/docs/modeling-your-data/modeling-your-data-with-dbt/migration-guides/agent-analytics/)
to back up the existing base and rewrite its 19 scalar columns in place, preserving
the incremental manifest and agent source lookup. This avoids reprocessing the
atomic history. The guide covers grants, table properties, validation and rollback.

A coordinated whole-package rebuild is an alternative when the required atomic
history is retained. Do not rebuild the base alone while retaining an advanced
manifest. New installations need no migration.
